    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=1,\\ y=0$ (or $x=0,\\ y=1$).",
      "worked": "Choose $y=0$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3&=1-0^3\\\\x&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are rational, and $1^3+0^3=1$. Hence $(x,y)=(1,0)$ is a solution; interchanging the variables gives $(0,1)$.",
